{"id": "EUVD-2026-86708", "enisaUuid": "4dccad06-2bc2-3d1f-821c-7e763da60e73", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nASoC: Intel: avs: Clean up the bus when fetching ML caps fails\n\nsnd_hdac_ext_bus_get_ml_capabilities() may fail and its return code\nshall be checked and accounted for. Address the issue by updating the\nerror-path for avs_pci_probe().\n\nAt the same time, if the function in question succeeds but the next part\nof avs_pci_probe() fails, the hlink list shall be cleaned up before\nleaving the scope.", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T10:24:02", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:13:01", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/68885c606a6e41dd4d3fe72f11241a6a438246ed", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a16ca1987ce8666c13482437db21232d41600e3f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2d96325e8ed97ec70623f788c35cca5d68c34351", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/498bf26639e99a98e7a3db880a7da8251aaf4289", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/04447cd14ebcc924f2d745dd33b9506735bda5b4", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/559ea14b7ae7c7562b48759fa545b64958f35b73"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98055", "GHSA-38h3-q9xp-263p"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "3e06d695-9bcd-3447-896f-042a5f78ba53", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1affc44ea5dd554c103e0ce1e809f3aa5d942349 <68885c606a6e41dd4d3fe72f11241a6a438246ed"}, {"id": "4cc17e89-dbdf-3996-838e-4168b64f006b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1affc44ea5dd554c103e0ce1e809f3aa5d942349 <a16ca1987ce8666c13482437db21232d41600e3f"}, {"id": "6099f7b5-4193-3ffd-9a09-4e1f052cac17", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.7"}, {"id": "7d0b97a4-2d04-387e-8415-ee0351b76fbd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1affc44ea5dd554c103e0ce1e809f3aa5d942349 <04447cd14ebcc924f2d